From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:20:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: Report the Shader Model 6 features by default.

Unreal Engine 5 games check for feature level 12_1, Shader Model 6,
resource binding tier 3, wave ops and 64-bit atomics before they choose
their Shader Model 6 path, and needed DXMT_D3D12_SM6=1 to start. Report
them unless DXMT_D3D12_SM6=0, which brings back Shader Model 5.1,
feature level 11_1, binding tier 2, no wave ops and no 64-bit atomics
for a game whose Shader Model 6 path fails. Only CheckFeatureSupport's
answers change; the translator doesn't, so translated shaders and their
cache key stay the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.cpp | 2 +-
 src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.hpp | 6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.cpp b/src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.cpp
index 96cb8db..965bab6 100644
--- a/src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.cpp
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ bool DXILCaptureMode() {
 
 bool
 SM6Caps() {
-  static const bool on = DXILCaptureMode() || env::getEnvVar("DXMT_D3D12_SM6") == "1";
+  static const bool on = DXILCaptureMode() || env::getEnvVar("DXMT_D3D12_SM6") != "0";
   return on;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.hpp b/src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.hpp
index c18662a..5ff3393 100644
--- a/src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.hpp
+++ b/src/d3d12/d3d12_dxil_dump.hpp
@@ -13,11 +13,13 @@ void DumpDXIL(const D3D12_SHADER_BYTECODE &Bytecode);
 
 // True when DXMT_DXIL_DUMP is set. The device then reports what Unreal Engine's SM6 check needs (feature level 12_1,
 // shader model up to 6.7, binding tier 3, wave ops, 64-bit atomics), so SM6-only games get as far as creating their
-// DXIL pipelines, which are captured and fail with E_NOTIMPL. For capture runs only: such a game can't render.
+// DXIL pipelines, which are captured; a pipeline using an op the translator lacks fails with E_NOTIMPL.
 bool DXILCaptureMode();
 
 // Report what Shader Model 6 games check for (feature level 12_1, SM 6.7, binding tier 3, wave ops, 64-bit atomics):
-// in capture mode, or with DXMT_D3D12_SM6=1. (MacNeutron)
+// by default, so Unreal Engine 5 games start. DXMT_D3D12_SM6=0 reports SM 5.1, feature level 11_1, binding tier 2,
+// no wave ops and no 64-bit atomics again, for a game whose SM6 path fails; capture mode always reports SM6.
+// (MacNeutron)
 bool SM6Caps();
 
 // Capture mode also saves each root signature as <folder>/rs-<FNV-1a 64>.bin, and appends one line per pipeline to
-- 
